//
// Agent control protocol, contract version 0.2.2.
//
// The controller compiles a test configuration into one Plan per agent. Each
// agent dials the controller, so an agent behind NAT or in a cloud needs no
// inbound port. The controller serves ControllerService over gRPC with mutual
// TLS, and agents are its clients. An agent first calls Register and then
// keeps one bidirectional Session stream open. The controller sends Prepare,
// Start, and Stop commands down the stream, and the agent sends heartbeats,
// command results, and counter snapshots up the stream. The canonical JSON
// form of a Plan is the proto3 JSON mapping of the Plan message, which the
// standalone agent mode reads from a file. See contracts/README.md for the
// state machines, the error codes, and the digest rules.
//
// Version 0.2.0 adds the UpdateRates, StartCapture, and StopCapture commands
// and the signature fields of ModuleRef. It only adds fields and messages, so
// an agent of version 0.1.0 and a controller of version 0.2.0 still register
// and run plans. The controller sends the new commands only to an agent whose
// Capabilities.engine_api is 0.2.0 or later.
//
// Version 0.2.1 adds ModuleRef.settings, the module settings of a plan. It
// only adds a field. An agent of version 0.2.0 ignores the field, so the
// controller sends a plan with module settings only to an agent whose
// Capabilities.engine_api is 0.2.1 or later.
//
// Version 0.2.2 adds the download of a finished capture file: the
// FetchCapture command on the Session stream and the UploadCapture RPC, which
// the agent opens on its own connection when the controller asks. It only adds
// a command, an RPC, and messages. The controller sends FetchCapture only to
// an agent whose Capabilities.engine_api is 0.2.2 or later.

